  "notes": "The formal/medical term for childbirth. Used primarily in medical contexts, official documents, and news reporting. In everyday conversation, {出産|しゅっさん} or {産|う}む is far more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自然|しぜん}{分娩|ぶんべん}: natural childbirth\n- {無痛|むつう}{分娩|ぶんべん}: painless delivery (epidural birth)\n- {分娩|ぶんべん}{室|しつ}: delivery room\n- {分娩|ぶんべん}{台|だい}: delivery bed\n- {分娩|ぶんべん}{予定日|よていび}: expected delivery date\n- {異常|いじょう}{分娩|ぶんべん}: abnormal delivery, complicated birth\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出産|しゅっさん}: childbirth, giving birth — the standard general-purpose word\n- お{産|さん}: childbirth — casual, warm, and commonly used in everyday speech\n- {産|う}む: to give birth — the verb form\n- {陣痛|じんつう}: labor pains, contractions — specifically the pain during labor",
